# Feature modules

One folder per business area: **`src/features/<feature>/`**.

## Standard layout

```text
src/features/<feature>/
  domain/              # types, zod schemas, pure helpers
  repositories/        # *Repository — apiJson only
  usecases/            # *UseCase — one file per operation
  controllers/           # use*Controller.ts hooks
  views/               # *Page.view.tsx — UI only
  components/          # feature-specific (maps, dialogs)
  lib/                 # optional pure utils (e.g. map geometry)
```

## Naming

- Use cases: `list-vehicles.usecase.ts`, `add-vehicle.usecase.ts`
- Controllers: `fleet-page.controller.ts` → `useFleetPageController`
- Views: `fleet-page.view.tsx` → `FleetPageView`
- Repositories: `vehicles.repository.ts` → `vehiclesRepository` export

## Cross-feature calls

- Prefer **use case → repository** in the owning feature.
- If feature B needs feature A data, call **A’s use case** from B’s controller — not B’s repository reaching into A’s API paths ad hoc.
- Shared types live in **domain** or `src/types/` when used by 3+ features.

## Feature-specific UI

- Heavy UI (maps, charts) stays in `features/<feature>/components/`.
- Do not put feature business logic in `src/components/ui/`.

## New feature checklist

1. Types in `domain/`
2. Repository methods
3. Use cases per API operation
4. Controller hook + view model type
5. View component
6. `app/.../page.tsx`
7. `queryKeys` entries in `@/lib/query-keys`
